# revenge-vblood.vrs: revenge D20 and D21's purge (Session 1, after revenge.vrs). On rv-test0 (rv-test's copy with
# playerCooldownMinutes 0; rv-test disabled), Chaos kills a native Faction_Bandits V Blood (${VB} at mark ${VBMARK}) with
# `.devkill`: VBloodKilled is raised (a native V Blood, D30), "revenge rv-test0: vblood kill +10 heat" and, with heat 6,
# the player is due at once; the revenge starts outside the territory. During tier 2 `.nyar purge confirm` ends it with
# "revenge rv-test0 ended: purge" and no private line, then "tracked units: 0" and "revenge: 0 heat rows, 0 due".
# Needs: the step 2 Release DLL; NyarDevTools and DevChatEcho; rv-test0 enabled, rv-test, bw-test and every FactionKills
# definition disabled; no purge cooldown running. Run: --var VBMARK=<mark> --var VB=<guid>
ensure
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
console TPHome
wait 3
chat .nyar event reload
expect-log events: reloaded
chat .nyar event disable rv-test
expect-reply rv-test
chat .nyar event enable rv-test0
expect-reply rv-test0
chat .devgo ${VBMARK}
expect-log \[DEV TP\] ${VBMARK}
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
mark
chat .devkill ${VB} 80 1
expect-log \[DEV KILL\] n=1
expect-log trigger: VBloodKilled timeout=10
expect-log revenge rv-test0: vblood kill \+10 heat timeout=10
expect-log revenge rv-test0 due timeout=5
expect-log event rv-test0 started by Revenge timeout=15
expect-log spawned CHAR_Bandit_Thug for rv-test0 timeout=30
expect-chat The Bandits come for you
shot chat rv0-start
wait 4
chat .devkill -301730941 40
expect-log event rv-test0 wave 1 cleared timeout=20
expect-log spawned CHAR_Bandit_Hunter for rv-test0 timeout=40
wait 4
mark
chat .nyar purge
expect-reply purge confirm
chat .nyar purge confirm
expect-log revenge rv-test0 ended: purge timeout=10
expect-log purge: 1 events ended timeout=5
expect-no-log revenge is spent timeout=10
wait 20
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0
chat .nyar event info rv-test0
expect-reply revenge: 0 heat rows, 0 due
shot chat rv0-purge
